---
<Base title={"Questions to Ask a Home Battery or Generator Installer | HomeBackupCost"} description={"Questions to ask a home battery or standby generator installer before you sign: license, permits, what is included, warranty, and who handles inspection."} schema={[{ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage', mainEntity: faq.map(([q,a]) => ({ '@type':'Question', name:q, acceptedAnswer:{ '@type':'Answer', text:a } })) }]}>
<h1>Questions to ask a battery or generator installer</h1>
<p class="lede">Ask every installer the same questions so you can compare their quotes.</p>
<h2>License and permits</h2>
<ul><li>Is the electrical work done by a licensed electrician? What's the license number? (Check it on your state licensing board's website.)</li><li>Who pulls the permit and schedules the inspection?</li><li>For generators: who handles the gas or propane connection, and is that a licensed plumber or gas fitter?</li></ul>
<h2>Scope</h2>
<ul><li>Which circuits will be backed up: the whole home or a critical-loads panel?</li><li>Is a panel or service upgrade needed? Is it in this price?</li><li>What transfer equipment is used? The NEC (702.5) requires listed transfer or interconnection equipment for standby systems (<a href="https://up.codes/s/interconnection-or-transfer-equipment">UpCodes</a>, as of 2026-10-26).</li><li>Will you notify the utility, or is an interconnection application needed? (Required for batteries paired with solar.)</li></ul>
<h2>Price and warranty</h2>
<ul><li>Can I get an itemized quote listing equipment, labor, permits, pad, and trenching?</li><li>Who handles the equipment warranty and the labor warranty, and for how long?</li><li>For generators: what does annual maintenance cost?</li><li>What's the payment schedule? Avoid paying most of the price up front.</li></ul>
<p>Then <a href="/how-to-compare-backup-power-quotes/">compare quotes side by side →</a> and check <a href="/backup-power-installer-red-flags/">red flags →</a></p>
<p class="note"><a href="/quotes/"><strong>Get installer quotes →</strong></a> · <a href="/calculator/">Size your backup first with the calculator →</a></p>
<h2>FAQ</h2>
{faq.map(([q,a]) => <details class="card" style="margin-bottom:10px"><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}
